From: ghidra_rh850 project
Subject: [PATCH] sim: v850: stop aliasing the 1 MiB low address space

The V850 simulator maps 0x00000000..0x000fffff through a 32 KiB backing
store.  Loading a 1 MiB RH850/P1M-E CodeFlash image therefore makes every
0x8000-byte block overwrite the previous block.  Instruction reads at their
real CodeFlash addresses see bytes from the final alias rather than the loaded
firmware.

This repository supports the RH850 v850e3v5 target, whose CodeFlash image uses
the complete 1 MiB low address range.  Give that range a full-size backing
store so each CodeFlash address remains distinct.  A 1 MiB modulo over a 1 MiB
region preserves the existing region command while removing the aliases.
---
 sim/v850/v850-sim.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sim/v850/v850-sim.h b/sim/v850/v850-sim.h
index e96f965664d..00000000000 100644
--- a/sim/v850/v850-sim.h
+++ b/sim/v850/v850-sim.h
@@ -46,6 +46,6 @@ extern SIM_DESC simulator;
 
 
-#define V850_ROM_SIZE 0x8000
+#define V850_ROM_SIZE 0x100000
 #define V850_LOW_END 0x200000
 #define V850_HIGH_START 0xffe000
 
